keywords:
  - "modularity"
  - "information hiding"
  - "separation of concerns"
  - "boundary objects"
  - "namespace collision"
  - "declarative registry"
  - "reproducible review"
  - "open science"
abstract: >-
  A thin reader that declares what a set of small evaluative instruments
  is, reads whichever sibling packages are installed, and checks one
  narrow property: that no two of them have given the same spelling to
  different things. It adds no instrument of its own and computes no
  aggregate; a legible reading says only that the declared vocabularies
  did not overlap.
